@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-nouns`
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-reading`
IMPORT `ca-interpretation-definitions`

-- ca-tests-definitions.l4
--
-- The defined terms of section 2(1) and section 35(1), as pass 2 encodes them.
-- Expected values are written from the text of the Act, before the module was run.
-- Three kinds of expected value appear.
--   * TRUE: the term is named by the definition, or the stated condition is met.
--   * FALSE: the definition says "means" (the whole meaning), or it says "does not include", or the text says the condition fails.
--   * `#ASSERT REFUSED`: the definition says "includes" (it does not say nothing else is covered), or the case is one the text does not address.
-- A zone, a record, or a list is checked field by field with the words the text uses.

§ `Section 2(1) and section 35(1): where the definitions apply`

-- "In this Act," (section 2(1)): the words define terms for the Act itself.
#ASSERT `a definition of section 2(1) applies` `in the Interpretation Act itself`
-- The text does not say whether they reach another enactment, or anything that is not an enactment.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a definition of section 2(1) applies` `in another enactment`)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a definition of section 2(1) applies` `somewhere that is not an enactment`)
-- "In every enactment," (section 35(1)), unless a contrary intention appears (section 3(1)); the Act applies to its own interpretation (section 3(2)).
#ASSERT `a definition of section 35(1) applies` `in another enactment` `unless` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a definition of section 35(1) applies` `in another enactment` `unless` TRUE)
#ASSERT `a definition of section 35(1) applies` `in the Interpretation Act itself` `unless` FALSE
#ASSERT `a definition of section 35(1) applies` `in the Interpretation Act itself` `unless` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a definition of section 35(1) applies` `somewhere that is not an enactment` `unless` FALSE)

§ `Section 2(1) and section 35(1): the one rule for reading a definition`

-- A definition that says "means" gives the whole meaning; one that says "includes" does not; a pointer lists no members.
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Act in section 2(1)`) `covers` "an Act of Parliament"
#ASSERT NOT (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Act in section 2(1)`) `covers` "a regulation")
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term enact`) `covers` "issue"
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term enact`) `covers` "repeal")
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term military`) `covers` "the police")
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term military`) `covers` "all or any part of the Canadian Forces"

§ `s 2(1) "Act"`

-- "Act means an Act of Parliament."
#ASSERT (`the definition of the term Act in section 2(1)`'s `how it speaks`) EQUALS `means`
#ASSERT `is an Act within section 2(1)` `an Act of Parliament`
#ASSERT NOT (`is an Act within section 2(1)` `an Act of a legislature`)
#ASSERT NOT (`is an Act within section 2(1)` `a regulation`)
#ASSERT NOT (`is an Act within section 2(1)` `a portion of an Act of Parliament`)
#ASSERT NOT (`is an Act within section 2(1)` `a portion of a regulation`)
#ASSERT NOT (`is an Act within section 2(1)` `an instrument of none of these kinds`)

§ `s 2(1) "enact"`

-- "enact includes to issue, make or establish."
#ASSERT (`the definition of the term enact`'s `how it speaks`) EQUALS `includes`
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term enact`) `covers` "issue"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term enact`) `covers` "make"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term enact`) `covers` "establish"
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term enact`) `covers` "amend")

§ `s 2(1) "enactment"`

-- "enactment means an Act or regulation or any portion of an Act or regulation."
#ASSERT `is an enactment within section 2(1)` `an Act of Parliament`
#ASSERT `is an enactment within section 2(1)` `a regulation`
#ASSERT `is an enactment within section 2(1)` `a portion of an Act of Parliament`
#ASSERT `is an enactment within section 2(1)` `a portion of a regulation`
-- "Act" means an Act of Parliament (section 2(1)); an Act of a legislature is therefore not one.
#ASSERT NOT (`is an enactment within section 2(1)` `an Act of a legislature`)
#ASSERT NOT (`is an enactment within section 2(1)` `an instrument of none of these kinds`)
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term enactment`) `covers` "a regulation"
#ASSERT NOT (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term enactment`) `covers` "a by-law of a municipality")

§ `s 2(1) "public officer"`

-- "public officer includes any person in the federal public administration who is authorized by or under an enactment to do or enforce
-- the doing of an act or thing or to exercise a power, or on whom a duty is imposed by or under an enactment."
#ASSERT `is a public officer within section 2(1) where` TRUE `and is authorized` TRUE `or has a duty imposed` FALSE
#ASSERT `is a public officer within section 2(1) where` TRUE `and is authorized` FALSE `or has a duty imposed` TRUE
#ASSERT `is a public officer within section 2(1) where` TRUE `and is authorized` TRUE `or has a duty imposed` TRUE
-- In the federal public administration but neither authorized nor charged with a duty: "includes" does not say.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`is a public officer within section 2(1) where` TRUE `and is authorized` FALSE `or has a duty imposed` FALSE)
-- FORK F-PUBLIC-OFFICER: outside the federal public administration the text does not say, whether authorized or charged with a duty.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`is a public officer within section 2(1) where` FALSE `and is authorized` TRUE `or has a duty imposed` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`is a public officer within section 2(1) where` FALSE `and is authorized` FALSE `or has a duty imposed` TRUE)

§ `s 2(1) "repeal"`

-- "repeal includes revoke or cancel."
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term repeal`) `covers` "revoke"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term repeal`) `covers` "cancel"
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term repeal`) `covers` "suspend")

§ `s 35(1) "Act"`

-- "Act, in respect of an Act of a legislature, includes a law of the Legislature of Yukon, of the Northwest Territories or for Nunavut."
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Act in an enactment, in respect of an Act of a legislature`) `covers` "a law of the Legislature of Yukon"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Act in an enactment, in respect of an Act of a legislature`) `covers` "a law of the Legislature of the Northwest Territories"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Act in an enactment, in respect of an Act of a legislature`) `covers` "a law of the Legislature for Nunavut"
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Act in an enactment, in respect of an Act of a legislature`) `covers` "a law of the Legislature of Ontario")

§ `s 35(1) "bank"`

-- "bank means a bank listed in Schedule I or II to the Bank Act."
#ASSERT `is a bank within section 35(1) if` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`is a bank within section 35(1) if` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term bank`) `covers` "a bank listed in Schedule I or II to the Bank Act"
#ASSERT NOT (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term bank`) `covers` "a credit union")
#ASSERT (`the definition of the term bank`'s `what it points at`) EQUALS JUST "the Bank Act"

§ `s 35(1) "broadcasting"`

-- "broadcasting means any radiocommunication in which the transmissions are intended for direct reception by the general public."
#ASSERT `is broadcasting within section 35(1) where` TRUE `and` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`is broadcasting within section 35(1) where` TRUE `and` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`is broadcasting within section 35(1) where` FALSE `and` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`is broadcasting within section 35(1) where` FALSE `and` FALSE)

§ `s 35(1) "Canada"`

-- "Canada, for greater certainty, includes the internal waters of Canada and the territorial sea of Canada."
#ASSERT (`the definition of the term Canada`'s `how it speaks`) EQUALS `for greater certainty, includes`
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Canada`) `covers` "the internal waters of Canada"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Canada`) `covers` "the territorial sea of Canada"
-- FORK F-CANADA-EEZ: the definition does not say whether the exclusive economic zone of Canada is part of Canada.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Canada`) `covers` "the exclusive economic zone of Canada")

§ `s 35(1) "Canadian waters"`

-- "Canadian waters includes the territorial sea of Canada and the internal waters of Canada."
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Canadian waters`) `covers` "the territorial sea of Canada"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Canadian waters`) `covers` "the internal waters of Canada"
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Canadian waters`) `covers` "the exclusive economic zone of Canada")

§ `s 35(1) "Clerk of the Privy Council or Clerk of the Queen’s Privy Council"`

-- "Clerk of the Privy Council or Clerk of the Queen’s Privy Council means the Clerk of the Privy Council and Secretary to the Cabinet."
#ASSERT elem "Clerk of the Privy Council" (`the definition of the term Clerk of the Privy Council`'s `the terms`)
#ASSERT elem "Clerk of the Queen’s Privy Council" (`the definition of the term Clerk of the Privy Council`'s `the terms`)
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Clerk of the Privy Council`) `covers` "the Clerk of the Privy Council and Secretary to the Cabinet"
#ASSERT NOT (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Clerk of the Privy Council`) `covers` "the Deputy Clerk of the Privy Council")

§ `s 35(1) "Commonwealth and Dependent Territories"`

-- "Commonwealth and Dependent Territories means the several Commonwealth countries and their colonies, possessions, dependencies,
-- protectorates, protected states, condominiums and trust territories."
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Commonwealth and Dependent Territories`) `covers` "the several Commonwealth countries"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Commonwealth and Dependent Territories`) `covers` "their colonies"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Commonwealth and Dependent Territories`) `covers` "possessions"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Commonwealth and Dependent Territories`) `covers` "dependencies"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Commonwealth and Dependent Territories`) `covers` "protectorates"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Commonwealth and Dependent Territories`) `covers` "protected states"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Commonwealth and Dependent Territories`) `covers` "condominiums"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Commonwealth and Dependent Territories`) `covers` "trust territories"
#ASSERT NOT (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Commonwealth and Dependent Territories`) `covers` "a foreign protectorate of another state")
#ASSERT (`the definition of the term Commonwealth and Dependent Territories`'s `what it points at`) EQUALS JUST "Commonwealth"

§ `s 35(1) "contiguous zone"`

-- (a) in relation to Canada: "the contiguous zone of Canada as determined under the Oceans Act".
#ASSERT (`the contiguous zone in relation to` `Canada as a state`)'s `what it is` EQUALS "the contiguous zone of Canada"
#ASSERT (`the contiguous zone in relation to` `Canada as a state`)'s `how it is fixed` EQUALS "as determined under the Oceans Act"
#ASSERT (`the contiguous zone in relation to` `Canada as a state`)'s `what it also includes` EQUALS EMPTY
-- (b) in relation to any other state: "as determined in accordance with international law and the domestic laws of that other state".
#ASSERT (`the contiguous zone in relation to` `a state other than Canada`)'s `what it is` EQUALS "the contiguous zone of the other state"
#ASSERT (`the contiguous zone in relation to` `a state other than Canada`)'s `how it is fixed` EQUALS "as determined in accordance with international law and the domestic laws of that other state"

§ `s 35(1) "continental shelf"`

#ASSERT (`the continental shelf in relation to` `Canada as a state`)'s `what it is` EQUALS "the continental shelf of Canada"
#ASSERT (`the continental shelf in relation to` `Canada as a state`)'s `how it is fixed` EQUALS "as determined under the Oceans Act"
#ASSERT (`the continental shelf in relation to` `a state other than Canada`)'s `what it is` EQUALS "the continental shelf of the other state"
#ASSERT (`the continental shelf in relation to` `a state other than Canada`)'s `how it is fixed` EQUALS "as determined in accordance with international law and the domestic laws of that other state"

§ `s 35(1) "contravene"`

-- "contravene includes fail to comply with."
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term contravene`) `covers` "fail to comply with"
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term contravene`) `covers` "evade")

§ `s 35(1) "county"`

-- "county includes two or more counties united for purposes to which the enactment relates."
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term county`) `covers` "two or more counties united for purposes to which the enactment relates"
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term county`) `covers` "a single county")

§ `s 35(1) "diplomatic or consular officer"`

-- "diplomatic or consular officer includes an ambassador, envoy, minister, chargé d’affaires, counsellor, secretary, attaché, consul-general,
-- consul, vice-consul, pro-consul, consular agent, acting consul-general, acting consul, acting vice-consul, acting consular agent, high
-- commissioner, permanent delegate, adviser, acting high commissioner, and acting permanent delegate" (twenty-one, counted from the text).
#ASSERT count (`the definition of the term diplomatic or consular officer`'s `what it names`) EQUALS 21
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term diplomatic or consular officer`) `covers` "ambassador"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term diplomatic or consular officer`) `covers` "chargé d’affaires"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term diplomatic or consular officer`) `covers` "pro-consul"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term diplomatic or consular officer`) `covers` "acting consular agent"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term diplomatic or consular officer`) `covers` "acting permanent delegate"
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term diplomatic or consular officer`) `covers` "trade commissioner")

§ `s 35(1) "exclusive economic zone"`

-- (a) in relation to Canada: "the exclusive economic zone of Canada as determined under the Oceans Act and includes the seabed and subsoil below that zone".
#ASSERT (`the exclusive economic zone in relation to` `Canada as a state`)'s `what it is` EQUALS "the exclusive economic zone of Canada"
#ASSERT (`the exclusive economic zone in relation to` `Canada as a state`)'s `how it is fixed` EQUALS "as determined under the Oceans Act"
#ASSERT elem "the seabed and subsoil below that zone" ((`the exclusive economic zone in relation to` `Canada as a state`)'s `what it also includes`)
-- (b) in relation to any other state: the text adds nothing about the seabed and subsoil.
#ASSERT (`the exclusive economic zone in relation to` `a state other than Canada`)'s `what it also includes` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT (`the exclusive economic zone in relation to` `a state other than Canada`)'s `how it is fixed` EQUALS "as determined in accordance with international law and the domestic laws of that other state"

§ `s 35(1) "Governor, Governor General or Governor of Canada"`

-- "Governor, Governor General or Governor of Canada means the Governor General of Canada or other chief executive officer or administrator
-- carrying on the Government of Canada on behalf and in the name of the Sovereign, by whatever title that officer is designated."
#ASSERT count (`the definition of the term Governor`'s `the terms`) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Governor`) `covers` "the Governor General of Canada"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Governor`) `covers` "other chief executive officer or administrator carrying on the Government of Canada on behalf and in the name of the Sovereign, by whatever title that officer is designated"
#ASSERT NOT (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Governor`) `covers` "the Prime Minister")

§ `s 35(1) "Governor General in Council or Governor in Council"`

-- "means the Governor General of Canada acting by and with the advice of, or by and with the advice and consent of, or in conjunction with
-- the Queen’s Privy Council for Canada."  The last argument is the F-QUEENS fact: the body is the Privy Council for Canada, however styled.
#ASSERT `the Governor General is the Governor in Council when acting` `by and with the advice of` `with a body for which` TRUE
#ASSERT `the Governor General is the Governor in Council when acting` `by and with the advice and consent of` `with a body for which` TRUE
#ASSERT `the Governor General is the Governor in Council when acting` `in conjunction with` `with a body for which` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the Governor General is the Governor in Council when acting` `without` `with a body for which` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Governor General is the Governor in Council when acting` `by and with the advice of` `with a body for which` FALSE)
#ASSERT elem "Governor in Council" (`the definition of the term Governor in Council`'s `the terms`)
#ASSERT elem "Governor General in Council" (`the definition of the term Governor in Council`'s `the terms`)

§ `s 35(1) "Great Seal"`

-- "Great Seal means the Great Seal of Canada."
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Great Seal`) `covers` "the Great Seal of Canada"
#ASSERT NOT (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Great Seal`) `covers` "the seal of a province")

§ `s 35(1) "Her Majesty, His Majesty, the Queen, the King or the Crown"`

-- Five expressions, one meaning: "the Sovereign of the United Kingdom, Canada and Her or His other Realms and Territories, and Head of the Commonwealth".
#ASSERT count (`the definition of the term Her Majesty`'s `the terms`) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT elem "the Crown" (`the definition of the term Her Majesty`'s `the terms`)
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Her Majesty`) `covers` "the Sovereign of the United Kingdom, Canada and Her or His other Realms and Territories, and Head of the Commonwealth"
#ASSERT NOT (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Her Majesty`) `covers` "the Governor General of Canada")

§ `s 35(1) "Her Majesty’s Realms and Territories or His Majesty’s Realms and Territories"`

-- "means all realms and territories under the sovereignty of Her or His Majesty."
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Her Majesty’s Realms and Territories`) `covers` "all realms and territories under the sovereignty of Her or His Majesty"
#ASSERT NOT (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Her Majesty’s Realms and Territories`) `covers` "a territory under the sovereignty of another state")
#ASSERT count (`the definition of the term Her Majesty’s Realms and Territories`'s `the terms`) EQUALS 2

§ `s 35(1) "herein"`

-- "herein used in any section shall be understood to relate to the whole enactment, and not to that section only."
#ASSERT (`the definition of the term herein`'s `how it speaks`) EQUALS `shall be understood to relate to`
#ASSERT `the reach of the word herein, used in any section,` EQUALS `the whole enactment`
#ASSERT NOT (`the reach of the word herein, used in any section,` EQUALS `the section in which it is used, only`)
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term herein`) `covers` "the whole enactment, and not to that section only"
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term herein`) `covers` "the section in which it is used")

§ `s 35(1) "holiday"`

-- "holiday means any of the following days, namely, Sunday; New Year’s Day; Good Friday; Easter Monday; Christmas Day; the birthday or the
-- day fixed by proclamation for the celebration of the birthday of the reigning Sovereign; Victoria Day; Canada Day; the first Monday in
-- September, designated Labour Day; National Day for Truth and Reconciliation, which is observed on September 30; Remembrance Day; any day
-- appointed by proclamation to be observed as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving; and ..."
#ASSERT `a day of the kind` `a Sunday` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` FALSE
#ASSERT `a day of the kind` `New Year’s Day` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` FALSE
#ASSERT `a day of the kind` `Good Friday` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` FALSE
#ASSERT `a day of the kind` `Easter Monday` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` FALSE
#ASSERT `a day of the kind` `Christmas Day` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` FALSE
#ASSERT `a day of the kind` `Victoria Day` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` FALSE
#ASSERT `a day of the kind` `Canada Day` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` FALSE
#ASSERT `a day of the kind` `Labour Day, the first Monday in September` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` FALSE
#ASSERT `a day of the kind` `the National Day for Truth and Reconciliation, September 30` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` FALSE
#ASSERT `a day of the kind` `Remembrance Day` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` FALSE
#ASSERT `a day of the kind` `a day appointed by proclamation to be observed as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` FALSE
-- FORK F-HOLIDAY-BIRTHDAY: "the birthday or the day fixed by proclamation": taken, each is a holiday.
#ASSERT `a day of the kind` `the birthday of the reigning Sovereign` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` FALSE
#ASSERT `a day of the kind` `the day fixed by proclamation for the celebration of the birthday of the reigning Sovereign` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` FALSE
-- The text lists Sunday and not Saturday, and lists no other day: "means any of the following days".
#ASSERT NOT (`a day of the kind` `a Saturday` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a day of the kind` `any other day` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` TRUE)
-- (a) in any province, a day the lieutenant governor appoints by proclamation, or a non-juridical day by an Act of the legislature;
-- (b) in any city, town, municipality or other organized district, a civic holiday appointed by resolution.
#ASSERT `a day of the kind` `a day appointed by proclamation of the lieutenant governor of a province to be observed as a public holiday or as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving within the province` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` TRUE
#ASSERT `a day of the kind` `a non-juridical day by virtue of an Act of the legislature of a province` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` TRUE
#ASSERT `a day of the kind` `a day appointed to be observed as a civic holiday by resolution of the council or other authority charged with the administration of the civic or municipal affairs of a city, town, municipality or other organized district` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` TRUE
-- Where the thing is to be done in another place the text does not say.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a day of the kind` `a day appointed by proclamation of the lieutenant governor of a province to be observed as a public holiday or as a day of general prayer or mourning or day of public rejoicing or thanksgiving within the province` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a day of the kind` `a non-juridical day by virtue of an Act of the legislature of a province` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`a day of the kind` `a day appointed to be observed as a civic holiday by resolution of the council or other authority charged with the administration of the civic or municipal affairs of a city, town, municipality or other organized district` `is a holiday under section 35(1) where` FALSE)

§ `s 35(1) "internal waters"`

-- (a) in relation to Canada: "the internal waters of Canada as determined under the Oceans Act and includes the airspace above and the bed
-- and subsoil below those waters".
#ASSERT (`the internal waters in relation to` `Canada as a state`)'s `what it is` EQUALS "the internal waters of Canada"
#ASSERT (`the internal waters in relation to` `Canada as a state`)'s `how it is fixed` EQUALS "as determined under the Oceans Act"
#ASSERT elem "the airspace above those waters" ((`the internal waters in relation to` `Canada as a state`)'s `what it also includes`)
#ASSERT elem "the bed and subsoil below those waters" ((`the internal waters in relation to` `Canada as a state`)'s `what it also includes`)
-- (b) in relation to any other state: "the waters on the landward side of the baselines of the territorial sea of the other state".
#ASSERT (`the internal waters in relation to` `a state other than Canada`)'s `what it is` EQUALS "the waters on the landward side of the baselines of the territorial sea of the other state"
#ASSERT (`the internal waters in relation to` `a state other than Canada`)'s `what it also includes` EQUALS EMPTY

§ `s 35(1) "legislative assembly or legislature"`

-- "legislative assembly or legislature includes the Lieutenant Governor in Council and the Legislative Assembly of the Northwest Territories,
-- as constituted before September 1, 1905, and the Legislature of Yukon, of the Northwest Territories or for Nunavut."
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term legislature`) `covers` "the Lieutenant Governor in Council"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term legislature`) `covers` "the Legislative Assembly of the Northwest Territories, as constituted before September 1, 1905"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term legislature`) `covers` "the Legislature of Yukon"
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term legislature`) `covers` "the Legislature of the Northwest Territories"
