§ `s 35(1) "lieutenant governor"`

-- "in Yukon, the Northwest Territories and Nunavut means the Commissioner"; elsewhere the lieutenant governor or other chief executive
-- officer or administrator carrying on the government of the province indicated by the enactment.
#ASSERT `the office meant by lieutenant governor in` Yukon EQUALS "the Commissioner"
#ASSERT `the office meant by lieutenant governor in` `the Northwest Territories` EQUALS "the Commissioner"
#ASSERT `the office meant by lieutenant governor in` Nunavut EQUALS "the Commissioner"
#ASSERT `the office meant by lieutenant governor in` Ontario EQUALS "the lieutenant governor or other chief executive officer or administrator carrying on the government of the province indicated by the enactment, by whatever title that officer is designated"
#ASSERT `the office meant by lieutenant governor in` `Prince Edward Island` EQUALS "the lieutenant governor or other chief executive officer or administrator carrying on the government of the province indicated by the enactment, by whatever title that officer is designated"

§ `s 35(1) "lieutenant governor in council"`

-- (a) a province: the lieutenant governor acting with the executive council; (b) Yukon: the Commissioner of Yukon acting with the consent of
-- the Executive Council of Yukon; (c) the Northwest Territories: likewise; (d) Nunavut: the Commissioner.
#ASSERT `the person meant by lieutenant governor in council in` Alberta EQUALS "the lieutenant governor of the province indicated by the enactment acting by and with the advice of, by and with the advice and consent of, or in conjunction with, the executive council"
#ASSERT `the person meant by lieutenant governor in council in` Quebec EQUALS "the lieutenant governor of the province indicated by the enactment acting by and with the advice of, by and with the advice and consent of, or in conjunction with, the executive council"
#ASSERT `the person meant by lieutenant governor in council in` Yukon EQUALS "the Commissioner of Yukon acting with the consent of the Executive Council of Yukon"
#ASSERT `the person meant by lieutenant governor in council in` `the Northwest Territories` EQUALS "the Commissioner of the Northwest Territories acting with the consent of the Executive Council of the Northwest Territories"
#ASSERT `the person meant by lieutenant governor in council in` Nunavut EQUALS "the Commissioner"

§ `s 35(1) "military"`

-- "military shall be construed as relating to all or any part of the Canadian Forces."
#ASSERT (`the definition of the term military`'s `how it speaks`) EQUALS `shall be construed as relating to`
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term military`) `covers` "all or any part of the Canadian Forces"

§ `s 35(1) "oath"`

-- "oath includes a solemn affirmation or declaration when the context applies to any person by whom and to any case in which a solemn
-- affirmation or declaration may be made instead of an oath, and in the same cases the expression sworn includes the expression
-- “affirmed” or “declared”."
#ASSERT `oath includes a solemn affirmation or declaration where` TRUE
#ASSERT `sworn includes affirmed or declared where` TRUE
-- Where no affirmation or declaration may be made instead of an oath the text does not say.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`oath includes a solemn affirmation or declaration where` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`sworn includes affirmed or declared where` FALSE)

§ `s 35(1) "Parliament"`

-- "Parliament means the Parliament of Canada."
#ASSERT `the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Parliament`) `covers` "the Parliament of Canada"
#ASSERT NOT (`the term defined by` (`the definition of the term Parliament`) `covers` "the Parliament of the United Kingdom")

§ `s 35(1) "person"`

