§ `s 35(1) "writing"`

-- "writing, or any term of like import, includes words printed, typewritten, painted, engraved, lithographed, photographed or represented or
-- reproduced by any mode of representing or reproducing words in visible form."
#ASSERT `writing, section 35(1), includes words in the mode` `words printed`
#ASSERT `writing, section 35(1), includes words in the mode` `words typewritten`
#ASSERT `writing, section 35(1), includes words in the mode` `words painted`
#ASSERT `writing, section 35(1), includes words in the mode` `words engraved`
#ASSERT `writing, section 35(1), includes words in the mode` `words lithographed`
#ASSERT `writing, section 35(1), includes words in the mode` `words photographed`
#ASSERT `writing, section 35(1), includes words in the mode` `words represented or reproduced by another mode of representing or reproducing words in visible form`
-- "includes" does not say that words not in visible form are outside writing.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`writing, section 35(1), includes words in the mode` `words that are not in visible form`)

§ `Section 3(1): the Act applies to every enactment, by kind of instrument`

-- Every provision applies to every enactment unless a contrary intention appears.  The kinds of enactment are those of section 2(1):
-- an Act (of Parliament), a regulation, and a portion of either.
#ASSERT `the provisions of the Act apply to an instrument of the kind` `an Act of Parliament` `unless` FALSE
#ASSERT `the provisions of the Act apply to an instrument of the kind` `a regulation` `unless` FALSE
#ASSERT `the provisions of the Act apply to an instrument of the kind` `a portion of an Act of Parliament` `unless` FALSE
#ASSERT `the provisions of the Act apply to an instrument of the kind` `a portion of a regulation` `unless` FALSE
-- "Unless a contrary intention appears": where one does, the provision does not apply to that enactment.
#ASSERT NOT (`the provisions of the Act apply to an instrument of the kind` `an Act of Parliament` `unless` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the provisions of the Act apply to an instrument of the kind` `a regulation` `unless` TRUE)
-- An Act of a legislature is not an "Act" in the sense of section 2(1), so it is not an enactment; section 3(1) says nothing of whether the Act applies to it (#34, #677).
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the provisions of the Act apply to an instrument of the kind` `an Act of a legislature` `unless` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the provisions of the Act apply to an instrument of the kind` `an Act of a legislature` `unless` TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`the provisions of the Act apply to an instrument of the kind` `an instrument of none of these kinds` `unless` FALSE)
-- The test of what an enactment is is the one section 2(1) gives for "enactment", and it says no to an Act of a legislature.
#ASSERT NOT (`is an enactment within section 2(1)` `an Act of a legislature`)
